Yes. Run these read-only checks in Administrator CMD. They won't activate/deactivate Office or change anything.

1. Check KMS configuration

cscript "C:\Program Files\Microsoft Office\root\Office16\ospp.vbs" /dstatusall | findstr /i "KMS KMSHost LICENSE STATUS"

2. Check for Office activation services/tasks

schtasks /query /fo LIST /v | findstr /i "KMS OfficeActivator AutoKMS Office"

3. Check for common activation-tool files

dir C:\ /a /s /b 2>nul | findstr /i "KMSAuto AutoKMS KMSPico OfficeActivator"

How I'll interpret it

No KMS/task/tool evidence + OOB_GRACE → likely just an unactivated Office installation.

KMS server configured / KMS activation task / AutoKMS/KMSPico files → strong evidence an activation workaround was used.

LICENSED with a genuine Retail/OEM key → potentially legitimate perpetual activation.


